<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador monetary base up 5.5 pct at Feb 7.</title>
<headline>Ecuador monetary base up 5.5 pct at Feb 7.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base grew 5.5 percent to 3.0 billion sucres in the week to February 7, the central bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In January 1997, monetary base fell 7.4 percent to 2.85 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The monetary base ended 1996 at 3.08 billion sucres, up from 2.41 billion sucres at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
